From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: debug v2 - the DSA assembler's VIOL detector (the loop hunt's refined instrument)

PROVENANCE: this line's debug instrument v2, 2026-11-06, on the composed
stack (absorb + fp8-pages + pagerows-fix). v1's SEL dump caught the fp8
selection's page-start attractor but its lines mixed stale scratch
(count=0 dense rows) with sparse rows and carried no causal horizon.
v2: print only count>0 rows, tag npool, and fire a VIOL line whenever
an E4M3 selection (pt==0, logical positions) contains a token beyond
the row's own causal limit (row[0] > q) - mechanically impossible
unless something selects beyond the scored range. bf16 (physical
page-row values) keeps the periodic SEL print only. Read-only printf
with a __syncwarp; no addressing change. Sorts last (glm-zz-*).
OWNER: this line; STATUS: the loop hunt's instrument v2.

diff --git a/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_ops.cu b/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_ops.cu
index b2fbee106..4c8205953 100644
--- a/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_ops.cu
+++ b/zig/kernels/cuda/glm_ops.cu
@@ -25,6 +25,16 @@ extern "C" __global__ void tf_glm_dsa_tokens(const long long* __restrict__ pools
         int tail = 0;
         for (int t = 0; t < 3; ++t) tail += npool * 4 + t <= q;
         counts[r] = npool > K ? 4 * K + tail : 0;
+        __syncwarp();
+        if (r == 0 && counts[r] > 0) {
+            if (pt == 0 && row[0] > (int)q)
+                printf("VIOL pos=%d npool=%d t0=%d t1=%d cnt=%d\n",
+                       *pos, (int)npool, row[0], row[1], counts[r]);
+            else if (((*pos) & 63) == 0)
+                printf("SEL pos=%d npool=%d cnt=%d t=[%d %d %d %d %d %d %d %d]\n",
+                       *pos, (int)npool, counts[r], row[0], row[1], row[2],
+                       row[3], row[4], row[5], row[6], row[7]);
+        }
     }
 }
 
